-- title:
--   Growth at slow points forces a uniform drop
-- statement:
--   Let $m\ge1$, $c>0$ and $0<q<1$. There is $n_0>4m$ with the following property. Let $w$ be a positive nonincreasing sequence with $w_n\le Dq^n$ for some $D$ and all $n$. Suppose that for every $n>4m$ with $w_{n-2m}\le2w_n$ we have $c\,w_n\le w_{2(n-2m)}$. Then
--   $$
--   2w_n<w_{n-2m}\qquad\text{for all }n\ge n_0 .
--   $$
--
--   The threshold $n_0$ depends only on $m$, $c$ and $q$, not on the sequence or on $D$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/SlowDrop.lean#L50-L95

